.TH CRYO 1 "" "cryo" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cryo \- compiler and build tool for the Cryo programming language
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cryo
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B cryo
.I file.cryo
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cryo
builds Cryo programs and libraries, from a single file or from a project
described by a
.I cryoconfig
file, and links them with the system's C compiler.
It finds its standard library and runtime beside its own binary.
.PP
.B cryo help
lists every command and option;
.B cryo help
.I command
describes one.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B build
Build a file or a cryoconfig project.
.TP
.B run
Build the project and run the program.
.TP
.B test
Build and run the project's tests.
.TP
.B check
Check a file for errors without generating code.
.TP
.B init
Create a new project.
.TP
.B version
Print the version;
.B \-\-verbose
also names the binary and the standard library it uses.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CRYO_CC
The C compiler that links programs, in place of the first of
.BR cc ,
.B gcc
and
.B clang
found on
.BR PATH .
.TP
.B XDG_CACHE_HOME
The archives a build makes for options the installed ones do not cover are
kept below
.IR $XDG_CACHE_HOME/cryo ,
or
.I ~/.cache/cryo
when it is unset.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cryolsp (1),
.UR https://cryolang.org
.UE
